@startuml AopConcepts
!theme plain
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 60
skinparam ranksep 50

package "ASPECT  (LoggingAspect class)\nThe cross-cutting module" #dce8ff {

  [**POINTCUT**\n────────────────────\nexecution(* service.*.*(..))\n\nExpression that answers:\nWHICH methods to intercept?] as pc #fffbcc

  [**ADVICE**\n────────────────────\n@Before          — runs before the call\n@After           — always after (finally)\n@AfterReturning  — only on success\n@AfterThrowing   — only on exception\n@Around          — wraps the whole call;\n                   the only kind that can\n                   change args / return value\n                   or skip the call entirely] as adv #d4f7d4
}

package "Target bean  (e.g. ServiceImpl)" #fff0ee {
  [**JOIN POINT**\n────────────────────\nA point in execution where\nan aspect CAN hook in.\nIn Spring AOP = always\na method invocation.] as jp #ffd6d6
}

pc -right-> jp : selects ▶
adv -right-> jp : fires at ▶

note bottom
  **WEAVING** = physically wiring the aspect into the target
  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Spring AOP  → runtime proxy created by BeanPostProcessor at startup
  Full AspectJ → compile-time or class-load-time, rewrites bytecode directly, no proxy
end note
@enduml
